#: ../../li3po4/vacancy-paths.rst:4
msgid "Li空孔の拡散経路"
msgstr "Li Vacancy Diffusion Paths"

#: ../../li3po4/vacancy-paths.rst:6
msgid ""
"Liの位置が1つ空いているとき、隣のLiはどの経路を通ってそこに移るでしょうか。\\ "
"3つの機械学習原子間ポテンシャルを使ってQuloudで求めた経路数は、UMAで31、SevenNetで30、CHGNetで20でした。\\ "
":numref:`li3po4-migration-paths` で、各モデルでどのLiサイトが経路で結ばれるかを比べます。"
msgstr ""
"When one Li site is vacant, what path does a neighboring Li atom take to "
"reach it? \\ With three machine-learning interatomic potentials in "
"Quloud, we obtained 31 paths with UMA, 30 with SevenNet, and 20 with "
"CHGNet. \\ :numref:`li3po4-migration-paths` compares which Li sites the "
"paths connect in each model."

#: ../../li3po4/vacancy-paths.rst:10
msgid ""
"隣のLiが空孔に移ると、そのLiがもといた位置が空くため、空孔はLiと逆向きに移ります。\\ "
"図の曲線は、このときLiがたどると計算された経路です。図を選ぶと元の大きさで確認できます。"
msgstr ""
"When a neighboring Li atom moves into a vacancy, it leaves its original "
"site empty, so the vacancy moves in the opposite direction to the Li "
"atom. \\ The curves show the calculated paths of the Li atoms during "
"these moves. You can select the figure to view it at its original size."

#: ../../li3po4/vacancy-paths.rst:15
msgid "12個のLiサイトを結ぶ移動経路。左のUMAと中央のSevenNetは右のCHGNetより経路が多い"
msgstr ""
"Migration paths connecting 12 Li sites. UMA on the left and SevenNet in "
"the center have more paths than CHGNet on the right."

#: ../../li3po4/vacancy-paths.rst:20
msgid ""
"Li空孔の移動に対応するLiの経路。左からUMAの31経路（橙）、SevenNetの30経路（緑）、CHGNetの20経路（灰色）。\\ "
"青い球と数字はLiサイト、Pで始まる番号は経路、紫の多面体はPO₄四面体を表します。"
msgstr ""
"Paths taken by Li atoms as Li vacancies migrate. From left to right: 31 "
"paths for UMA (orange), 30 for SevenNet (green), and 20 for CHGNet "
"(gray). \\ Blue spheres and numbers mark Li sites, labels starting with P"
" identify paths, and purple polyhedra represent PO₄ tetrahedra."

#: ../../li3po4/vacancy-paths.rst:23
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"UMAとSevenNetでは広い範囲に分岐した経路が見えます。CHGNetでは経路の数が少なく、結ばれるサイトの組み合わせも異なります。\\ "
"経路数には、候補の選び方や経路が成立するかどうかの判定が影響します（技術ノートの\\ `端点・経路の候補・イメージの数 <https"
"://technical-notes.quemix.com/electronic/neb.html#neb-path-"
"setup>`__）。また、Liの移動しやすさは経路ごとの障壁にも左右されます。 :numref:`{number}. {name} "
"<li3po4-doc-vacancy-barriers>` では、図に示した経路の障壁を比較します。"
msgstr ""
"With UMA and SevenNet, the paths branch across a wide region. CHGNet "
"gives fewer paths and connects different pairs of sites. \\ The path "
"count depends on how candidate paths are selected and the criteria for "
"deciding whether a path exists (see \\ `endpoints, candidate paths, and "
"number of images <https://technical-notes.quemix.com/electronic/neb.html"
"#neb-path-setup>`__ in the Technical Notes). How easily Li moves also "
"depends on the barrier along each path. In :numref:`{number}. {name} "
"<li3po4-doc-vacancy-barriers>`, we compare the barriers along the paths "
"shown here."

#: ../../li3po4/vacancy-paths.rst:26
msgid ""
"文献では、32原子の不規則構造で3.5 Å未満のLiサイト間を候補とし、46経路を調べました。\\ 両端のサイトを結ぶ\\ `最低エネルギー経路 "
"<https://technical-notes.quemix.com/electronic/neb.html#minimum-energy-"
"path>`__\\ を求める\\ `NEB（nudged elastic band）法 <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/electronic/neb.html#nudged-elastic-band>`__\\ "
"を用い、同じ構造・同じサイトの組み合わせでNNPとDFTの経路の位置と形が近いことを確かめています。 `Liらの図5 "
"<https://doi.org/10.1063/1.4997242>`__"
msgstr ""
"Li et al. considered Li sites less than 3.5 Å apart in a 32-atom "
"disordered structure and examined 46 paths. \\ To find the \\ `minimum "
"energy paths <https://technical-notes.quemix.com/electronic/neb.html"
"#minimum-energy-path>`__ \\ connecting the endpoints, they used the \\ "
"`nudged elastic band (NEB) method <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/electronic/neb.html#nudged-elastic-band>`__ \\ and "
"confirmed that the NNP and DFT paths were similar in position and shape "
"for the same structure and pairs of sites. `Li et al., Fig. 5 "
"<https://doi.org/10.1063/1.4997242>`__"

#: ../../li3po4/vacancy-paths.rst:30
msgid "まとめ"
msgstr "Summary"

#: ../../li3po4/vacancy-paths.rst:32
msgid ""
"3つのモデルで、Liサイトを結ぶ経路の数とつながり方が異なりました。\\ "
"文献とは元の原子配置が異なるため、本計算の経路の再現性を評価するには、同じ構造と始点・終点でOpenMXによるDFT-"
"NEB計算を行い、経路の形と障壁を照合する必要があります。"
msgstr ""
"The three models gave different numbers of paths and different "
"connections between Li sites. \\ Because our starting atomic arrangement "
"differs from that of Li et al., assessing the reproducibility of our "
"paths requires running DFT-NEB calculations with OpenMX on our structure "
"with the same endpoints, then comparing path shapes and barriers."

